{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560251-converting-w-ta-to-storypath","id":1560251,"title":"Converting W:tA to Storypath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-28T22:35:03-07:00","id":1560251,"title":"Converting W:tA to Storypath","content":"I had some sketched-up ideas for how to go about this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Forms - various forms enjoy scale/advantage and enhancement in certain areas.</span><br /> <br /> Homid: Enhancement to passing unnoticed through crowds of humans or in the city.<br /> <br /> Glabro: +1 Durability and Might; +1 to Power for attacks relying on muscle power. Enhancement to hiding in urban locales where no or minimal humans are present and attacking in confined spaces. +1 Leadership on attempts to frighten or terrify humans, or resist the same from humans.<br /> <br /> Crinos: +2 Durability and Might; +2 Power for attacks relying on muscle power. Enhancement to close combat damage; Aggravated, Brutal, and Deadly tags for claw attacks (just agg for bites); minimal Enhancement for running. +3 Leadership on attempts to frighten or terrify humans, or resist the same from humans. Uses the Collateral Damage rules from TC: Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Hispo: +2 Durability, +1 Might, +1 Speed, +1 Power for attacks relying on muscle power (+2 for bites); Aggravated, Brutal, and Deadly tags for bite attacks; Enhancement for running and jumping. Same Leadership adjustment as Crinos. Also uses the Collateral Damage rules from TC: Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Lupus: +1 Durability, +2 Speed, +1 Power for bite attacks, Enhancement for running and jumping (the highest for running), as well as hiding in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> This adapts the concept of forms being for purposes in Forsaken, but for war rather than the hunt. Homid is, naturally, good for &quot;passing through the herd&quot; unnoticed, while Glabro becomes a form that inspires wolfman cryptids lurking in abandoned buildings and cemeteries. Glabro becomes the iaijutsu draw with a relatively short katana to the ootachi murder spree of Crinos and Hispo. Lupus becomes superb for travel and wilderness concealment.<br /> <br /> As to how much Enhancement each form gets, I was considering tying that in to the changes I'd make to Renown, or perhaps Primal-Urge. And speaking of which...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Primal-Urge</span> - the Garou's connection to the whole of spirit and flesh that defines her existence. This starts at one, and increases via increases to Renown (now purchased). Glory, Honor, and Wisdom get three points divided among them, and like with facets of Inspiration in Trinity Continuum, improving a Renown category to 1, 3, or 5 grants an additional dot of PU. PU also determines how much Essence (not Gnosis) you have, at 5 + (PU x 2). Primal-Urge is also rolled to shapeshift, like in Storyteller W:tA (one success gets you across the five eventually, more successes will get you there speedier).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence</span> can be spent where Gnosis was for various mystical purposes, often Gifts, as well as to get Rage effects, provided the werewolf has a high enough Rage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Rage</span> is kind of like anima levels from EX3, in that there are several discrete levels of it that generally provide progressively greater potential effects when you spend Essence to utilize default Rage Essence effects. Its only point of similarity to Hunger in V5 is that, unlike anima levels, it is rarely, if ever, at 0, because all Garou and Fera can discern that something is wrong with the world (obviously, Ananasi and Nuwisha are a bit of an exception) and are frequently put off by that pervasive presence of loathing.<br /> <br /> Rage 0: Calm. How are you so calm? No extra actions for you, but you can instantly assume any form (1 Essence)<br /> <br /> Rage 1: Angry. You can ignore negative conditions for a turn, and may make an additional attack (either one, 1 Essence each).<br /> <br /> Rage 2: Furious. You can make up to two additional attacks per turn (same price) or gain Enhancement to an attack (1 Essence per point, maximum = Rage level).<br /> <br /> Rage 3: Frenzy. You can make up to three additional attacks per turn (same price), ignore being Unconscious (1 Essence, for the scene) or make a Stamina + Survival roll to self-heal based on the value of the injuries that you're suffering from. Local werewolf too angry to die! Unfortunately, you also treat attempts to leave combat, stand down, or not pursue others to engage in violence as extremely difficulty, gaining a +3 (or more?) difficulty to do these things or other calm and peaceful endeavors. Failing to engage in a non-combat roll applies what successes you rolled to an attack, pursuit, or similarly aggressive roll instead.<br /> <br /> (I don't accept frenzy as something that needs to be a completely GM-controlled character event. RPGs moved past that in 2005 with Weapons of the Gods, and that book is legally able to drink in the US. But don't let it; it's out of print and getting pretty rare!)<br /> <br /> Rage can be lowered if you manage a (Composure + Integrity) roll against a difficulty of (Rage level + 1). On the other hand, threats to the Bonds of a Garou can also raise it (roll Bond rating at a difficulty of present Rage level + 1). Extra successes can &quot;spillover&quot; to lower or increase more than one level if there are enough successes left over to cover the difficulty of the next highest or lowest level. If a Garou experiences a drop to Rage 0, she automatically returns to Rage 1 at the end of the scene, unless a compelling, Bond-related reason exists for delaying that, but it will happen when she wakes up after sleeping if delayed in this manner.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Exposure</span>, also from TC: Aberrant, is also a concern. Assume that the circumstances where a covert game of Aberrant would result in being exposed instead result in a Veil Breach that needs addressing. Hispo actions build Exposure normally, while Crinos manages to build it with Enhancement, since even with the Delirium, the memory holes it leaves tend to be conspicuous to anyone who knows what to look for. And getting photographed? Better hope you learn to disable phones yesterday.<br /> <br /> (There are so many rules that cater to situations and play styles for W:tA in Storypath that I honestly wish we could just saw it off from the WoD and plant it in a Storypath game. It seems like it would fit better.)<br /> <br /> I'm undecided on character tier and TN, and I have pondered a few of the Gifts and how they interact with Renown. I think that borrowing the way that Inspiration and Facets work from TC helps to eliminate some of the dragging issues relating to Rage and having points of it or making rolls based off of it, especially the issue of &quot;venting&quot;, which here is not something you would necessarily want to do on account of how you're using Essence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quite predictably</span>, Breed, Auspice, and Tribe are a Garou's main three paths, which cover her Origin, Role, and Society, respectively. Pure Breed would become Legacy and add Enhancement to certain related social rolls, except for impressing people, which would experience it as a difficulty increase on account of how you're living in the shadow of your ancestors. Ancestors is something I'm still working on, and Spirit Heritage would be kind of like Legacy but its difficulty increase is in opposed spirit broods.<br /> <br /> Another miscellaneous note: Some Fera will have to find a new name for a Renown Category, because Cunning is an Attribute now. I'm thinking Guile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T12:47:30-07:00","id":1560291,"title":"","content":"So, I forgot about the concept of Complications while writing the above. So Rage 3 should just add a complication, as should Crinos (the former being much more than the latter, as in Crinos only has a Complication 1 while, as noted above, being in a frenzy is Complication 3).<br /> <br /> I had an idea to name the Crinos-born after one of the names of Hephaestus, but since they're associated with war, whatever crazed neo-classicist behind the names as they are within the setting might have also called them &quot;Areia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Homids get to choose &quot;normal&quot; origin paths as their origin; everyone else has specially-made paths for that.<br /> <br /> Rather than starting values, the differences mostly fall out of paths, though the higher Gnosis breeds might also do with an Essence recovery bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T05:09:46-07:00","id":1560338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560251-converting-w-ta-to-storypath?p=1560291#post1560291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I forgot about the concept of Complications while writing the above. So Rage 3 should just add a complication, as should Crinos (the former being much more than the latter, as in Crinos only has a Complication 1 while, as noted above, being in a frenzy is Complication 3).<br /> <br /> I had an idea to name the Crinos-born after one of the names of Hephaestus, but since they're associated with war, whatever crazed neo-classicist behind the names as they are within the setting might have also called them &quot;Areia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Homids get to choose &quot;normal&quot; origin paths as their origin; everyone else has specially-made paths for that.<br /> <br /> Rather than starting values, the differences mostly fall out of paths, though the higher Gnosis breeds might also do with an Essence recovery bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Areia, but Hephaestus works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T11:23:34-07:00","id":1560347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560251-converting-w-ta-to-storypath?p=1560338#post1560338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of Areia, but Hephaestus works too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it would be Hephaestus's epithets of Amphigyeeis or Kyllopodion, references to his being disabled, because of continued Garou prejudice against the breed's congenital impairment. A softened position on the breed using this sourcing, ironically, would be Polymetis (&quot;many devices&quot;, meaning shrewd or crafty). I wouldn't have them be sterile, but like ahi Nagah, they would be noticeably rarer results of Garou-Garou pairings. The first tenet as pre-W5 had it wouldn't be in place, in any case.<br /> <br /> Areia has a lot going for it for being brief, and emphasizing how growing up in Crinos would tend to cause a lot of fragile and important objects to break in the child's early life (as calmly handling things in Crinos comes with Complication 1).<br /> <br /> ()<br /> <br /> New Edges<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Ancestors (1 to 3)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">When adversity shows itself, you can call upon your ancestors for aid, and they will answer. Roll your Primal-Urge; each success allows you to increase a Skill rating by one for the scene or add a Skill Trick, or provide a clue based on the character\u2019s present predicament. The character may call upon this aid once per point per story.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Legacy (1 to 3)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Your family has a storied heritage to it, as members of a given tribe or, in the case of Fera, similar group. You show the signs of your tribe\u2019s associated physical appearance more strongly, and you have much to live up to... as well as more ancestor-spirits to potentially offend. Each point in Legacy grants an additional Leadership scale when dealing with Garou and Fera, but also adds 1 Complication if you act in a way that would be contrary to your ancestors\u2019 storied history. If you fail to buy off lower level Complications, this typically results in a punishment from your sept; at higher levels, it frequently entails ancestor-spirits letting you know their disapproval in ways ranging from instructing other spirits to avoid you to outright possession.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Pack Spirit Patron (1+)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Garou enjoys both membership in a pack and the guidance of a tutelary spirit avatar. The spirit patron provides a benefit to Traits, as well as being able to advise and occasionally act alongside the pack. The more dots that are invested in this Edge, the greater the advantage provided; there is no ceiling to how many dots a Garou can invest in this Edge.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Personal Spirit Patron (2+)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The character enjoys the patronage of a tutelary spirit avatar, made more difficult due to the pack-oriented nature of the Garou, making every dot in this Edge cost double. Note that a character cannot be in a pack or pack-like group and maintain this Edge. It is otherwise similar to Pack Spirit Patron in terms of mechanics.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Spirit Heritage (1 to 3)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Some relations between Changer and spirit are closer than merely exchanging chiminage. Through various means, you have a close, familial relationship with a given brood of spirits, and you gain Enhancement on rolls with these spirits equal to your Edge dots. Note that having this sort of relationship with banes or other Triatic servants will make most Gaian Garou extremely suspicious of you, at best.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}